cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research framework, please cite the associated NeurReps 2026 paper."
title: "NeurReps: Coordinate Factorization and Learned Geometry in Machine-Code Representations"
type: software
abstract: >-
  Research framework for evaluating information-equivalent coordinate factorizations
  of RISC-V machine code (SC, 4C, and 32C), including Conv1D training, raw-input
  accessibility probes, representation geometry, dataset controls, and matched
  eCFG counterfactual analyses.
